     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"></div></blockquote><div><br>Another variation of a Bernoulli model that will be wrong is: <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">stan_glmer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> binomial</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div></div></div>"
